# DotApp Frontend JS

Full reference: `AIRULES/09-DOTAPP-JS-AND-BRIDGE.md`, forms in `08-FORMS-AND-SECURITY.md`.

## Load order

1. `/assets/dotapp/dotapp.js` (router-generated keys)
2. Optional template/reactive
3. Module scripts

Bootstrap on `dotapp` event; register plugins on `dotapp-register` via `$dotapp().fn(...)`.

Custom FE libraries and jQuery ports: `AIRULES/09-DOTAPP-JS-AND-BRIDGE.md` §4 (playbook §4.C) and `AIRULES/examples/EX-15-dotapp-js-library.md`. Never edit `app/parts/js/`. Never edit `app/modules/DACore/` by default (informed exception: `AIRULES/00` §1). **MUST grep DACore (read-only) and this module first** — reuse an existing widget; do not write a second copy. Porting = rewrite vanilla + `$dotapp().fn` — do not wrap `$.fn.plugin`. If DACore already ships the widget, use it.

## Never

- `$.ajax` / `$.post` / `$.get` / raw `fetch` to DotApp endpoints (CRC/keys/signatures live in `$dotapp`)
- Assume getters always chain
- Skip CRC/CSRF by using raw `fetch` to secure endpoints
- `location.reload()` after `fo-rm` / `load` while staying on the page — patch `reply.html` + Notiflix toast (`AIRULES/09-DOTAPP-JS-AND-BRIDGE.md` §3)
- One `<fo-rm>` per row action — use `$dotapp().load()` + encrypted `data-*` (`AIRULES/08-FORMS-AND-SECURITY.md`)
- Leave a list/form clickable during `load()` — overlay until success **and** error (Notiflix preferred **or** module preloaders; desktop **and** mobile) (`AIRULES/09-DOTAPP-JS-AND-BRIDGE.md` §3)
- Dump users/logs/items with `->all()`, skip the pager because “few rows now”, or change pages by reloading `<a href="?page=">` / `location.reload()` — interactive AJAX pager + `$dotapp().load()` (`AIRULES/09-DOTAPP-JS-AND-BRIDGE.md` §3)
- Ship a catalog/articles list with no search, or filter `->all()` in JS — **ASK** in the plan; lookup lists **MUST** AJAX search (SQL + `paginate()`, 3+ chars)
- Invent a 2FA/OTP digit widget — use `$dotapp().twoFactor` (`AIRULES/09-DOTAPP-JS-AND-BRIDGE.md` §3)
- Delete with `alert()` / `window.confirm()` — graphical dialog first (`Notiflix.Confirm` on admin) (`AIRULES/09-DOTAPP-JS-AND-BRIDGE.md` §3)
- Public site: desktop-only header / hover menu / hide nav on mobile with no overlay drawer — L/R drawer, lock page scroll, scrollable drawer list, contacts+compact search in the drawer (`AIRULES/09-DOTAPP-JS-AND-BRIDGE.md` §3)
- Silent save / empty `.after()` / invent a second toast instead of grepping DACore — admin **toast**; public mark the field (`AIRULES/00` §2d)
- Skip step-up 2FA on a dangerous DACore action — `AIRULES/32-DACORE-RIGHTS.md` §6

jQuery `$` may coexist **for UI widgets** (ported datepickers, etc.). It must **not** send app requests. Prefer `$dotapp` for new DOM code. Register plugins with `$dotapp().fn(...)` on `dotapp-register`. When porting jQuery libraries, **ask**, then rewrite as `$dotapp().fn` (do not wrap `$.fn`). Playbook: `AIRULES/09-DOTAPP-JS-AND-BRIDGE.md` §4.C.

## Forms (preferred security — always for user POSTs)

HTML: `<fo-rm>` + `{{ formName(handler) }}` (not `f-form`). **MUST** put `formName` **between** `<fo-rm>` and `</fo-rm>` — never after `</fo-rm>`.  
Must load `/assets/dotapp/dotapp.js` first (injects random keys).  
Full sample: `AIRULES/examples/EX-01-secure-form-complete.md`.

```javascript
$dotapp().form('#saveForm')
  .before(function (data, form) {
    if ($dotapp(form).attr('blocked') == 1) return $dotapp().halt();
    $dotapp(form).attr('blocked', '1');
    $dotapp('#btn').attr('loading', 'true').attr('loader', 'dots');
    if (window.Notiflix && Notiflix.Block) Notiflix.Block.standard('#saveForm', 'Loading…');
  })
  .after(function (data, response, form) {
    var reply = $dotapp().parseReply(response);
    if (reply && reply.status == 1 && reply.html) $dotapp('#listInner').html(reply.html);
    $dotapp(form).attr('blocked', '0');
    $dotapp('#btn').removeAttr('loading').removeAttr('loader');
    if (window.Notiflix && Notiflix.Block) Notiflix.Block.remove('#saveForm');
  });
```

## AJAX

`$dotapp().load(url, method, data, ok, err)` — not raw fetch for DotApp secure APIs.

## Bridge

Template `{{ dotbridge:on(click)="fn(args)" }}` + `$dotApp->bridge->fn('fn', ...)`.
